            <ArticleTitle>Maintenance of pulpal vitality using potassium nitrate-polycarboxylate cement cavity liner.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>495-502</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Following deep restorations in vital teeth, postoperative pain of various durations frequently occurs, even if the teeth were asymptomatic before treatment. In this study, a potassium nitrate-polycarboxylate cement was used as a liner and was found clinically to tend to preserve pulpal vitality and significantly eliminate or decrease postoperative pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
